# ==========================================================
# CELL 1 - THE MODEL (v6: joint simultaneous multi-salt fit)
# ==========================================================
#
# v6 (on top of v5.2):
#
# JOINT SIMULTANEOUS FIT (FIT_MODE='joint', the new default). Specific
# conductivity is LINEAR in the ion-surface spline coefficients:
#     kappa_j = sum_i m_free_ij * W_i(T_j, sqrt I_j) / eta_j^alpha_i  + pairs_j
# so ALL seven ion surfaces are solved in ONE penalized weighted linear
# least-squares system:
#   - every salt equation constrains every ion it contains (Na+ is pinned
#     by NaCl AND Na2SO4 simultaneously - no sequential error cascade);
#   - the KCl transport-number rows enter as soft ANCHOR equations
#     lambda_K = t+ * kappa / m_free_K, fixing the cation/anion gauge that
#     whole-salt data alone cannot resolve;
#   - residuals are RELATIVE (each equation scaled by its measured kappa),
#     so dilute data is not drowned out by concentrated brines;
#   - smoothness via second-difference (P-spline) penalties per ion, one
#     global strength lambda chosen by K-fold cross-validation;
#   - cold rows (Mahboub NaCl/NH4Cl to -10 C) enter DIRECTLY as equations:
#     no known-ion Walden extrapolation is needed during training;
#   - held-out salts (K2SO4, MgSO4, CaSO4) NEVER enter the joint system -
#     the additivity tests stay non-circular.
# The sequential chain (v5.2) still runs first: it supplies the per-ion
# Walden alphas, the gauge initialization, and the seq-vs-joint comparison
# printout. Set FIT_MODE='sequential' to get exact v5.2 behavior.
#
# Retained from v5.2: AMBIENT_ONLY master pressure switch; wired source
# switches (Pan off); replicate policy (average within author, unit
# weights); CV-smoothed scattered splines for the sequential chain;
# relative-only Adams & Hall staging; unified speciation-conditions export;
# saturated-liquid viscosity branch (table to 623 K); all guards.

